A platform's own controller layout: SMS_PAD_DEFAULTS.

bindings.txt lines in an environment variable, read after the built-in
layout and before bindings.txt, so a platform can give its controller a
layout of its own (the Switch: R a soft spray, ZR the full one, - the
map) that a player's bindings.txt still changes.

--- a/platform/pad/pad.cpp
+++ b/platform/pad/pad.cpp
@@ -536,6 +536,10 @@
 	for (size_t i = 0; i < sizeof kDefaultPad / sizeof kDefaultPad[0]; i++)
 		g_pbind[kDefaultPad[i].control][g_npbind[kDefaultPad[i].control]++] = kDefaultPad[i].source;
 	parse_bindings(kDefaultBindings, "defaults");
+	// SMS_PAD_DEFAULTS: bindings.txt lines (\n between them) from the platform
+	// that runs the game, its own layout, before bindings.txt changes it
+	if (const char* platform = getenv("SMS_PAD_DEFAULTS"))
+		parse_bindings(platform, "SMS_PAD_DEFAULTS");
 	g_invert_cx = env_on("SMS_CAMERA_INVERT_X");
 	g_invert_cy = env_on("SMS_CAMERA_INVERT_Y");
 	if (g_invert_cx || g_invert_cy)
